<listitem><para><anchor id="test_1_test000040"/>TXN-SAGA-HARDENING-01: Circuit breaker opens after 5 consecutive failures. After the threshold, canAttempt() must return false.  </para>
</listitem>
<varlistentry><term>Member <ref refid="namespacethemis_1_1transaction_1_1test_1ab8441c453fc6e704181ca42e8ebe23b5" kindref="member">themis::transaction::test::TEST_F</ref>  (<ref refid="classthemis_1_1transaction_1_1test_1_1_transaction_wave_a_s_a_g_a_test" kindref="compound">TransactionWaveASAGATest</ref>, TxnSagaHardening02_IdempotentCompensation)</term></varlistentry>
<listitem><para><anchor id="test_1_test000041"/>TXN-SAGA-HARDENING-02: Idempotent compensation under concurrent retry storm. 10 concurrent threads each call compensate() for the same step; only one must succeed.  </para>
</listitem>
<varlistentry><term>Member <ref refid="namespacethemis_1_1transaction_1_1test_1a9bd4fcd4c674a83432da42cc1d082b4a" kindref="member">themis::transaction::test::TEST_F</ref>  (<ref refid="classthemis_1_1transaction_1_1test_1_1_transaction_wave_a_s_a_g_a_test" kindref="compound">TransactionWaveASAGATest</ref>, TxnSagaHardening03_PartialFailureOrdering)</term></varlistentry>
<listitem><para><anchor id="test_1_test000042"/>TXN-SAGA-HARDENING-03: Partial failure ordering — steps compensated in reverse order (last-executed first).  </para>
</listitem>
<varlistentry><term>Member <ref refid="namespacethemis_1_1transaction_1_1test_1a67b9b69fa91208298daa14f48e63b4af" kindref="member">themis::transaction::test::TEST_F</ref>  (<ref refid="classthemis_1_1transaction_1_1test_1_1_transaction_wave_a_s_a_g_a_test" kindref="compound">TransactionWaveASAGATest</ref>, TxnSagaHardening04_RetryStormBoundedBackoff)</term></varlistentry>
<listitem><para><anchor id="test_1_test000043"/>TXN-SAGA-HARDENING-04: Retry storm with bounded backoff stays within max retries and does not attempt after circuit opens.  </para>
</listitem>
<varlistentry><term>Member <ref refid="namespacethemis_1_1transaction_1_1test_1a68e3fef00f551a87b2dbfbb3305f9bea" kindref="member">themis::transaction::test::TEST_F</ref>  (<ref refid="classthemis_1_1transaction_1_1test_1_1_transaction_wave_a_timeout_test" kindref="compound">TransactionWaveATimeoutTest</ref>, TxnTimeout01_BackoffSchedule)</term></varlistentry>
<listitem><para><anchor id="test_1_test000044"/>TXN-TIMEOUT-01: Backoff schedule validation — base 100ms, factor 2×. First delay ≈ 100ms, second ≈ 200ms, third ≈ 400ms (within jitter tolerance).  </para>
</listitem>
<varlistentry><term>Member <ref refid="namespacethemis_1_1transaction_1_1test_1a84bae11dabf8153100c0bd8da5b8c6ee" kindref="member">themis::transaction::test::TEST_F</ref>  (<ref refid="classthemis_1_1transaction_1_1test_1_1_transaction_wave_a_timeout_test" kindref="compound">TransactionWaveATimeoutTest</ref>, TxnTimeout02_MonotonicExpectedValues)</term></varlistentry>
<listitem><para><anchor id="test_1_test000045"/>TXN-TIMEOUT-02: Delays must increase monotonically in expected-value terms (stochastic; seed 42 provides deterministic outcome).  </para>
</listitem>
<varlistentry><term>Member <ref refid="namespacethemis_1_1transaction_1_1test_1a044340a2033a8a2abe90843c0a8d8a92" kindref="member">themis::transaction::test::TEST_F</ref>  (<ref refid="classthemis_1_1transaction_1_1test_1_1_transaction_wave_a_timeout_test" kindref="compound">TransactionWaveATimeoutTest</ref>, TxnTimeout03_JitterBoundsStatistical)</term></varlistentry>
